---
layout: default
title: Freediving trains life
---

<div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16">
  <header class="mx-auto mb-16 max-w-3xl text-center">
    <p class="mb-4 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400">The practice</p>
    <h1 class="mb-5 mt-0 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight sm:text-6xl">Freediving trains life.</h1>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">The water makes attention physical. What happens between a body signal and your reaction is the real training.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="prose mx-auto mb-16 max-w-3xl text-left text-lg">
    <h2>Meditation with honest feedback</h2>
    <p>A freedive has clear signals: relaxation, pressure, equalization, buoyancy, the urge to breathe, the turn and the recovery breath.</p>
    <p>During training, notice each signal early. Relax what can relax. Equalize before pressure builds. Turn on the plan.</p>
    <p>The dive is complete when the diver surfaces with reserve and finishes recovery breathing calmly.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-16">
    <div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="mb-4 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400">The mental ladder</p>
      <h2 class="mb-4 mt-0 text-3xl font-black sm:text-4xl">From one point to the whole field.</h2>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Molchanovs builds the mental side wave by wave. Each step has a clear practice.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="rounded-2xl border border-current/10 p-6">
        <p class="mb-2 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400">Wave 1</p>
        <h3 class="mb-3 mt-0 text-2xl font-black">Body scan &amp; visualization</h3>
        <p class="mb-0 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Scan the body before the dive. Rehearse the dive route, the turn and the recovery breath.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-2xl border border-current/10 p-6">
        <p class="mb-2 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400">Wave 2</p>
        <h3 class="mb-3 mt-0 text-2xl font-black">Mindfulness</h3>
        <p class="mb-0 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Notice breath, heartbeat, contractions and thought. Keep attention on the next action.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-2xl border border-current/10 p-6">
        <p class="mb-2 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400">Wave 3</p>
        <h3 class="mb-3 mt-0 text-2xl font-black">Attention deconcentration</h3>
        <p class="mb-0 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Widen attention from one point into a field. See the periphery. Hear the soundscape. Feel the body at once.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-2xl border border-current/10 p-6">
        <p class="mb-2 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400">Wave 4</p>
        <h3 class="mb-3 mt-0 text-2xl font-black">Pressure practice</h3>
        <p class="mb-0 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Use a repeatable start ritual, simple self-talk and a clear focus for the dive.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-16 rounded-2xl bg-sky-950 p-8 text-slate-100 sm:p-10">
    <p class="mb-4 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-sky-400">Train with us</p>
    <h2 class="mb-4 mt-0 text-3xl font-black sm:text-4xl">The advanced work starts early.</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-300">Body, technique and attention are taught as one practice. Official Molchanovs training runs through Wave 2. The advanced attention practices are shared separately; these sessions do not issue Wave 3 or Wave 4 certification.</p>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-300">One person. One buoy. Your own pace and mental space. Someone fully watching.</p>
    <a href="https://t.me/firedev" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="mt-3 inline-flex min-h-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-sky-500 px-6 py-3 text-base font-bold text-slate-950 no-underline transition hover:bg-sky-400 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-white">Get in touch</a>
  </section>

  <aside class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-300/60 bg-amber-50 p-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-amber-950 dark:border-amber-300/20 dark:bg-amber-950/30 dark:text-amber-100">
    <p class="mb-2 font-black">Breath-hold safety is not a mental trick.</p>
    <p class="mb-0">Never train in water alone and never hyperventilate before a dive. Every in-water session uses an active, qualified buddy, conservative limits and a clear decision to surface with reserve.</p>
  </aside>
</div>
